(11)\qquad \unsure{\mathcal E}_{X/Y}^{T}=\operatorname{Ker}\bigl(\mathcal E_X^{T}\unsure{\mathrel{\text{---}}|\longrightarrow}\mathcal E_Y^{T}\bigr)
\]
we have a functor in \inserted{\unsure{the triple}} $(T\unsure{\mathrel{\text{---}}|\longrightarrow}X\longrightarrow Y)$ as variable. In particular: $\mathcal E_{X/Y}^{\unsure{\xi|\zeta}}$, $\unsure{\xi|\zeta}$ a geometric $p^t$ of $X$, $\mathcal E_{X/Y}^{\Omega}$, $\mathcal E_{X/A}^{\widetilde X}$ (if $Y=\operatorname{Spec} A$), $\mathcal E_{B/A}^{\widetilde B}$ $\ldots$

\margin{\uline{Note well} $\mathcal E_{X/Y}^T$, for $T$ variable, $X/Y$ fixed, is defined up to non-unique \unsure{!} isomorphism, and is denoted $\mathcal E_{X/Y}$ \unsure{simpl\textsuperscript{y}.}}

